{"companyInfo": {"Updated": "7/28/26", "Footnote": "Market value as of July 13, 2026.", "Country/Territory": "U.S.", "Headquarters": "Arlington, Va.", "Industry": "Aerospace & Defense", "CEO": "Robert K. Ortberg", "Website": "https://www.boeing.com", "Ticker": "BA", "Company type": "Public", "Revenues ($M)": "$89,463", "Profits ($M)": "$2,235", "Market value ($M)": "$169,887", "Number of employees": "182,000", "StockQuote": "NYSE"}, "description": "Boeing, together with its subsidiaries, designs, develops, manufactures, sells, services, and supports commercial jetliners, military aircraft, satellites, missile defense, plus human spaceflight and launch systems worldwide. The company operates through its commercial airplanes; defense, space, and security; and global services segments. In recent years, safety concerns and labor disputes have plagued the company, which was once lauded for its engineering-first culture. Boeing was incorporated in 1916. After a long history outside Seattle, in 2001 it moved its headquarters to Chicago to be closer to customers. It ultimately moved again to Arlington, Va., where it\u2019s presently headquartered.", "dataTables": [{"changeHeader": "", "footnote": "", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "valueHeader": "", "values": [{"change": null, "title": "Sector", "value": "Aerospace & Defense"}, {"change": null, "title": "Culture rank", "value": "93"}, {"change": null, "title": "Process rank", "value": "139"}, {"change": null, "title": "Product rank", "value": "12"}]}, {"changeHeader": "", "footnote": "", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "valueHeader": "", "values": [{"change": null, "title": "Sector", "value": "Transport"}, {"change": null, "title": "Industry", "value": "Aerospace and Defense"}, {"change": null, "title": "Current All-Star Rank", "value": "-"}, {"change": null, "title": "Previous All-Star Rank", "value": "-"}, {"change": null, "title": "Industry Rank", "value": "7"}, {"change": null, "title": "Prev